Fork maintained at:

  https://github.com/ph-rui/COMTool

Modifications in this fork:

  - Live refresh of the serial port list while the port dropdown is open
    (500 ms polling on a background thread, coalesced to one scan at a time).
  - Fixed the no-port busy loop in Serial.detectSerialPortProcess and the
    stale "detecting" state that made later clicks unresponsive.
  - Port items store the real device path in Qt.UserRole instead of parsing
    the display text; added natural COM ordering, macOS /dev/cu.*
    deduplication, and richer per-port tooltips.
  - Auto-update points at this fork instead of upstream releases, so a
    custom build is not replaced by an upstream binary.
  - Added unit tests, design documentation, and a CI workflow for the
    port-list helpers.

This fork remains under LGPL-3.0. The complete corresponding source is
available in this repository. See the design document at
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-17-comtool-live-port-refresh-design.md.

Avalonia port
=============

The Avalonia/.NET port under avalonia/ additionally bundles the Noto Sans
Mono CJK SC font (Simplified Chinese), Regular and Bold:

  avalonia/src/COMTool.App/Assets/Fonts/NotoSansMonoCJKsc-Regular.otf
  avalonia/src/COMTool.App/Assets/Fonts/NotoSansMonoCJKsc-Bold.otf

  Copyright (c) 2017-2023 The Noto Project authors (Google)
  Licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1 (see the license text at
  avalonia/src/COMTool.App/Assets/Fonts/OFL-NotoSansMonoCJK-SC.txt).

  https://github.com/notofonts/noto-cjk (Sans/Mono, Simplified Chinese)

It is the terminal font on every platform so that latin and CJK cells are
shaped from one face grid and mixed-language lines keep one baseline.
